<title>KENYA: Kenya coffee prices rally at weekly auction.</title>
<headline>Kenya coffee prices rally at weekly auction.</headline>
<dateline>NAIROBI 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prices of quality Kenyan coffee rallied at the weekly auction on Tuesday, gaining up to $30 on a world shortage of good quality coffee, auction officials said.</p>
<p>Grade ABs averaged $439 per 50-kg compared with $403 last week while grade AAs sold at $451 from $417. Grade PBs averaged $450 from $402.</p>
<p>The Coffee Board of Kenya said it sold 35,480 60-kg bags of coffee against the 36,456 bags sold last week.</p>
<p>--Wambui Chege, Nairobi Newsroom ++254-2 330-261.</p>
